      "description": "Zero LOWER-LIMB malignancy records attached to the index inpatient visit (RestrictVisit). Narrowed 2026-08-12 from 443392 'Malignant neoplastic disease' (5,314 standard descendants, every cancer of every site) to 4177242 'Malignant tumor of lower limb' (250) -- a 21x tightening to the anatomy that actually causes a lower-extremity amputation: its descendants are sarcoma of femur/tibia/fibula, sarcoma of bone of foot, melanoma of the limb. The broad set combined with a +/-30d window excluded 302 of 935 (32%), because an elderly vascular admission routinely carries an unrelated active or historical cancer code. KNOWN GAP, accepted deliberately: a sarcoma coded with NO site (e.g. plain 'Osteosarcoma', 'Sarcoma of bone') sits outside the lower-limb tree and is not excluded, so a genuinely oncologic amputation coded that way stays in the cohort. Adding 443564 (bone, -> 455 concepts) or also 4311439 (sarcoma, -> 837) would close it at the cost of anatomically impossible sites; rejected 2026-08-12 in favour of anatomic precision. NOTE ALSO: 'attached to the amputation procedure' is NOT expressible -- OMOP's condition_occurrence has no procedure link, only visit_occurrence_id and visit_detail_id, so the visit IS the finest available scope.",
